WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:45.000
Open ReelCue. Read the in-app disclosure explaining screen access, local processing, and the ability to disable access.

00:45.000 --> 01:45.000
Choose “Skip for now”. Accessibility remains off. The Today screen remains usable and offers “Agree & open Settings” again.

01:45.000 --> 01:55.000
Choose “Agree & open Settings” after the repeated disclosure.

01:55.000 --> 02:45.000
Enable the test service. Android explains screen access and control; the user explicitly taps Allow.

02:45.000 --> 03:10.000
Return to ReelCue after granting access. Counts and limits remain on the device.

03:10.000 --> 03:25.000
The user selects “Lock all now” and opens YouTube to demonstrate manual-lock enforcement.

03:25.000 --> 04:05.000
AccessibilityService recognizes the locked app, returns to Home and shows the break screen. This is a user-selected manual lock; live Shorts counting is not shown.
